                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25d797a2-f742-3542-84a3-f35cf6341e42",
                        "entry_id": "690c3442-f82c-3ab7-800e-e9cb0bea6171",
                        "glosses": [
                            "源自官話的姓氏；變體形式 Jiang"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4190f400-30ba-4e90-9632-00df2ea06e2d",
                                "sense_id": "25d797a2-f742-3542-84a3-f35cf6341e42",
                                "text": "As early as August we had publicly withdrawn our opposition to consideration of this question and indicated our support of the concept of the \"two Chinas,\" Chiang Kai-shek's Republic of China on Taiwan and the Communist People's Republic of China, each to have membership in the world organization.\nIt had not been easy for me to take a position that would be so disappointing to our old friend and loyal ally, Chiang.",
                                "translation": "早在八月份，我们就公开撤回了反对审议此问题的立场，并表示支持“两个中国”的概念，即蒋介石在台湾建立的中华民国和中华人民共和国，两者都应成为世界组织的成员。对我而言，采取这样一个会令我们老朋友和忠实盟友蒋[介石]如此失望的立场并不容易。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "caa6d8d1-3393-402e-a53c-ca4244e1c2d4",
                                "sense_id": "25d797a2-f742-3542-84a3-f35cf6341e42",
                                "text": "When Chiang Kai-shek died in 1975, it was widely assumed that he had wanted to be buried someday on the mainland, although he is not known to have left any explicit instructions. His body was embalmed and placed in what is officially still a temporary mausoleum here, and the same was done with his son.\nIf the Chiang family has its way, as now seems likely, both former presidents of Taiwan will finally be buried next spring.",
                                "translation": "蒋介石于1975年去世时，尽管他并未留下任何明确的遗嘱，人们普遍认为他生前希望有朝一日葬于大陆。他的遗体经过防腐处理后安葬于一座至今在官方层面上仍为临时陵墓的墓穴中，他的儿子也同样如此。如果蒋家如愿以偿（目前看来很有可能），这两位台湾[中华民国]前总统将于明年春天最终下葬。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22cc095f-1967-4517-b2ac-f007b8eaf958",
                                "sense_id": "25d797a2-f742-3542-84a3-f35cf6341e42",
                                "text": "In the past few weeks, the Chinese Nationalist Party’s (KMT) mayoral candidate for Taipei Chiang Wan-an’s (蔣萬安) ancestry has come under attack by several pundits.\nSince Chiang threw his hat in the ring, he has been purporting himself as the descendant of the Chiang family to garner support from pan-blue voters.\nIn January, he said that his name “Wan-an” was given to him by his grandfather — former president Chiang Ching-kuo (蔣經國) — as a reminder of his ancestral roots. On more than one occasion, he stated that he has always been proud of being a Chiang, and that he would follow in his ancestors’ — Chiang Kai-shek (蔣介石) and Chiang Ching-kuo — footsteps to make Taiwan a better place. He further underscored this lineage by placing an artistic image of himself with Chiang Ching-kuo, side-by-side, on his mayoral campaign flags.",
                                "translation": "近几周来，国民党台北市长候选人蒋萬安的家族背景遭到多位评论员的质疑。自蒋[萬安]宣布参选以来，他一直标榜自己是蒋家后裔，以此争取泛蓝选民的支持。\n今年一月，他表示“萬安”这个名字是他祖父——前总统蒋经国——赐予他的，以此纪念他的家族渊源。他曾多次表示，自己一直以身为蒋家子弟为荣，并将追随先祖蒋介石和蒋经国的脚步，为台湾建设更美好的未来。为了进一步强调这一家族血统，他还将自己与蒋经国并肩而立的画像印在了竞选旗帜上。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
